innovating on the ServiceNow AI Platform.\n\n### Connect\n\nMeet fellow creators and gain insights from the community.\n\n### Design\n\nFind components, patterns, and resources to help you start designing experiences on the ServiceNow AI Platform.\n\n### Knowledge 2026\n\nDive into the moments from Knowledge 2026 that matter most. Hear from the leading voices in AI. All the wow. All on demand.\n\n### World Forum 2026\n\nCheck out 2026 dates and locations, and discover how you can put AI to work in a city near you.\n\n### Webinars\n\nBroaden your knowledge by registering for live and on demand ServiceNow webinars.\n\n### Community events\n\nFind live events for the ServiceNow community happening near you.\n\n### Livestream\n\nJoin live events showcasing product news, customer stories, and expert insights.\n\n### now[dev]26\n\nBuild real solutions with the engineers behind the platform.\n\n![worldforum promo image](/content/dam/servicenow-assets/public/en-us/images/company-events/world-forum/26/background/wf26-global-nav-promo-lg.png)\n\n### World Forum 2026\n\nPut AI to work in a city near you. Explore the latest innovations, hear from industry leaders, and experience AI firsthand at a complimentary World Forum event.\n\n### AI Agent Stories\n\nLearn how ServiceNow customers are putting AI to work.\n\n### HR Stories\n\nSee how organizations are improving self-service and delivering outstanding employee experiences.\n\n### CRM Stories\n\nDiscover how businesses enable self-service for customers and reduce resolution time.\n\n### Public Sector/Government Stories\n\nExplore ways to streamline operations, engage citizens, and empower employees.\n\n### Now on Now\n\nHear how ServiceNow uses ServiceNow.\n\n![FedEx logo](/content/dam/servicenow-assets/public/en-us/digital-graphics/ds-logos/white/logo-fedex-white.svg)\n\n### Featured customer story\n\nFor FedEx, 5M ServiceNow workflows a month help get work done.\n\n### AI\n\nInsights on AI strategy, automation, and the future of intelligent workflows.\n\n### CRM\n\nHow AI is changing the way businesses strengthen relationships with customers.\n\n### News & Events\n\nStay in the loop on announcements and happenings at ServiceNow.\n\n### People & Culture\n\nA look inside ServiceNow's culture, people, and what drives us.\n\n### All topics\n\nThe conversations shaping work; walk into every room a step ahead.\n\n![workflow promo image](/content/dam/servicenow-assets/public/en-us/workflow/images/workflow-nav-promo.jpg)\n\n### The CX Shift\n\nNew research from 34,000 voices reveals a widening gap between what customers want and what they get.\n\n### Community\n\nConnect with other customers to share tips, exchange resources, and solve problems together.\n\n### Get support\n\nDiscover answers, troubleshoot issues, and get expert help, all in our support center.\n\n### IT Service Management\n\nDeliver IT services to your users all through a single cloud-based platform.\n\n### Customer Service Management\n\nProvide customers the ability to communicate and receive support through multiple channels.\n\n### IT Operations Management\n\nGet visibility into infrastructure and services, prevent outages, and expand operational agility.\n\n### ServiceNow AI Platform\n\nAutomate processes and develop, run, and manage applications.\n\n### What’s new in AI experiences\n\nUse AI-based tools to prioritize and automate routine tasks, detect incidents, and surface insights.\n\n### ServiceNow AI Platform\n\nAutomate business processes, streamline app development, and manage digital infrastructure.\n\n### Customer Service Management\n\nDeliver exceptional service, empower customers, and enhance their experience.\n\n### IT Service Management\n\nStreamline IT service delivery, boost productivity, resolve issues, and enhance user satisfaction.\n\n### Employee Service Management\n\nStreamline onboarding, provide HR and IT support, and empower employees with digital workflows.\n\n### Telecommunications Service Management\n\nUnify telecom operations and deliver proactive care with quality and availability for services.\n\n### Governance, Risk, and Compliance\n\nBuild an integrated risk program, enhance decision-making, and improve performance with automation.\n\n### Security Operations\n\nAccelerate response and strengthen security posture with SecOps workflows.\n\n### Learn More\n\nStart your day with MyNow.\n\n### ServiceNow Impact™ success plans\n\nReceive long-term adoption guidance and support with an Impact success plan tailored to you.\n\n### Services\n\nImplement and optimize ServiceNow with expert help from ServiceNow and our partners.\n\n### Zurich\n\nConfidently extend AI across your enterprise.\n\n### Xanadu\n\nThe biggest ServiceNow AI release yet.\n\n### Washington D.C.\n\nTake work to the next level with smarter, faster, simpler experiences for everyone.\n\n### Find a partner\n\nConnect with a ServiceNow partner to reach your business goals.\n\n### Become a partner\n\nJoin our partner ecosystem. Choose the partner paths that best fit your expertise and experience.\n\n### Partner awards\n\nMeet the global ServiceNow partners leading the way in innovation and value for our customers.\n\n### Partner portal\n\nFind tasks, alerts, and information you need, all in one place.\n\n### Partner applications\n\nExplore innovative apps that extend and complement the ServiceNow AI Platform.\n\n### Careers\n\nMake your next career move with the fastest growing enterprise software company.\n\n### Investors\n\nExplore investor news and resources.\n\n### ServiceNow AI Research\n\nLearn how we keep innovation moving forward through our AI research team, labs, and partnerships.\n\n### Leadership\n\nMeet the ServiceNow leadership team.\n\n### Locations\n\nSee ServiceNow office locations around the world.\n\n### Newsroom\n\nServiceNow is making headlines. Find announcements, media kits, and more.\n\n### Analyst Reports\n\nGet expert insights from top industry analysts on ServiceNow.\n\n### Global impact\n\nJoin us to foster a more sustainable, fair, and ethical world.\n\n### Trust and compliance\n\nLearn the measures ServiceNow takes to keep your data secure and compliant.\n\n### ServiceNow Shop\n\nThe official home for ServiceNow gear. Get the latest styles today.\n\n![Company Collage](/content/dam/servicenow-assets/images/naas/company-collage.png)\n\nSales\n\n![Workflow contributor 3-D icon](https://delivery.servicenow.com/adobe/assets/urn:aaid:aem:cf2e71f8-1f0b-4d7a-a45d-050c680b0732/as/wf-workflow-contributor-single-author.png?width=640&preferwebp=true)\n\n“It was November 5th, 2003. I knew that we had to start a company before I became 50, because a 50-year-old can't start a company. So, at 49—November 24th is my birthday—we started,” says Fred Luddy, ServiceNow founder.\n\n \n\nHe began the company with a single laptop at a desk in his house. Although he founded the company alone, he couldn’t build it alone.\n\nIn fact, a handful of people believed so strongly in what Fred was doing that they volunteered their time to work with him, even though he couldn’t pay them. Some of those people are still here, which speaks volumes to the kind of employees who have set the precedent for who we are today.\n\n![Alt](https://delivery.servicenow.com/adobe/assets/urn:aaid:aem:639c54c6-055f-4ff0-9d24-cee527d57006/as/wf-how-servicenow-was-born-when-world-works.png?width=640&preferwebp=true&smartcrop=16-9)\n\nA collaborative culture\n\n \n\nTo Jay B., employee No. 28 after contracting for the company, working at ServiceNow was all about teamwork and communication.\n\n“When we started,\" he says, \"it was about how do we get together, have a good time, and do something meaningful. Those early days were amazing because there were only 10 of us, and we were a group of people who understood each other, who knew how to communicate, and who fed off of each other.”\n\n \n\nAbout 19 years later, ServiceNow has quadrupled in size from its humble beginnings. But one thing has remained the same: our commitment to putting customers first. \n\n \n\n“Our [culture](https://careers.servicenow.com/life-at-servicenow/) was that we were going to be humble, that we were to absolutely have integrity. We were going to be confident but never arrogant. And we were going to always listen to the customer,” Fred explains.\n\nA caring community\n\n \n\nHis former assistant, Carla G., employee No. 8—or the “OG” as she refers to herself—blazed a trail of her own at ServiceNow. “When I first started working here, I was the only female and Mexican. I was also part of a group of kids who were building this company with great camraderie”—a camraderie that has kept her at ServiceNow to this very day.\n\n“This is a community where we care a lot for each other, and I’m very proud of it.”\n\n \n\n“I look back on my time at ServiceNow and, career aside, I’ve met some of the most amazing people in my life,” adds Mark O., employee No. 37. \"I’m not just talking co-workers—the customers, partners from all around the world. I can't believe the level of integrity, intelligence, and talent that I’ve been exposed to.”\n\nWally M., employee No. 177, will never forget the advice he received on his first day at ServiceNow on April 26, 2010. “I tell new employees what I was told on my first day, ‘I hope this is the highlight of your career, and I hope you get everything you ever wished for at ServiceNow,’ because that’s what it’s been for me, the highlight of my career.”\n\n \n\nHear more from Fred and several early employees as they reminisce about the good old days, sharing their stories, aspirations, and pride for what ServiceNow has become today.\n\n \n\nCEO Bill McDermott couldn’t be prouder of the lasting impact each of these people has made on ServiceNow: “The original founders of the company, beginning with Fred, always had the customer as the first, second, and third priority. It’s that passion, it’s that differentiation around not only delivering around the